      "id": "tzrfhs1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6.1 Primary Memory (Main Memory)"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Primary Memory comprises RAM (Random Access Memory), ROM (Read Only Memory), and Cache Memory.",
        "RAM is volatile main memory used for active processing, whereas ROM is non-volatile memory storing startup instructions.",
        "Cache Memory acts as a high-speed buffer between the CPU and main memory to accelerate data retrieval.",
        "Secondary Memory consists of external storage devices used for persistent data retention.",
        "Understanding memory hierarchy and memory units is critical for comparing computer performance."
      ],
      "id": "20bsik8"
    },
